{# Printable QR label sheet — Avery L7159-compatible grid (A4, 24 labels of
   63.5 x 33.9 mm in 3 columns x 8 rows).

   Deliberately DOES NOT extend `pdf/layout.html.twig`: the common layout
   paints a fixed organization header and legal footer inside the page body,
   which would print across the top and bottom sticker rows. A label sheet
   must map the physical die-cut grid exactly, so this template owns its own
   skeleton and the @page margins ARE the sheet margins.

   Geometry (Avery L7159 / J8159): label 63.5 x 33.9 mm, horizontal pitch
   66 mm (2.5 mm gutter between columns), vertical pitch 33.9 mm (no gap
   between rows), side margins (210 - 3*63.5 - 2*2.5) / 2 = 7.25 mm,
   top/bottom margins (297 - 8*33.9) / 2 = 12.9 mm.

   dompdf pitfalls this geometry depends on — each one silently breaks the grid
   (locked by DompdfEquipmentLabelSheetRendererTest, which measures the rendered
   positions):
   - NEVER a universal `* { margin: 0 }` reset: dompdf stores the @page margins
     on the root frame's style, so the universal rule overwrites them and the
     sheet starts at 0,0. Reset `body` only.
   - NEVER `table-layout: fixed`: dompdf 3.1 records every cell width as 0 in
     fixed layout and splits the table into equal columns, ignoring the
     63.5 / 2.5 mm widths.
   - Widths are CONTENT-box: a cell's padding is added on top of its `width`
     (QR cell: 24 + 3 + 0.9 = 27.9 mm).
   - `padding: 0` sits on the outer cell classes, not on `table.sheet td`, whose
     descendant selector would also override the inner label cells' padding.
   - A bounded, absolute text descendant keeps long values out of table sizing
     and page-break checks. The non-absolute content owns max-height and clipping;
     dompdf does not apply max-height to an absolutely positioned block.

   Expects in context:
   - lang: two-letter translation language (catalog domain "pdf")
   - labels: list of { qrDataUri, type, subType?, serialNumber?, facilityName?, locationLabel? }
     (`qrDataUri` is injected by the renderer adapter from each row's `qrValue`) #}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="{{ lang }}">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <title>{{ 'equipmentLabels.title'|trans({}, 'pdf', lang) }}</title>
  <style>
    @page { margin: 12.9mm 7.25mm; }
    body { margin: 0; font-family: DejaVu Sans, sans-serif; color: #09090b; }

    table.sheet { border-collapse: collapse; width: 195.5mm; }
    table.sheet td { border: none; vertical-align: top; }
    td.label { width: 63.5mm; height: 33.9mm; padding: 0; overflow: hidden; }
    td.gutter { width: 2.5mm; padding: 0; }
    .page-break { page-break-after: always; }

    table.label-inner { border-collapse: collapse; width: 63.5mm; }
    table.label-inner td { border: none; vertical-align: middle; }
    td.qr-cell { width: 24mm; padding: 3mm 0.9mm 3mm 3mm; }
    td.qr-cell img { width: 24mm; height: 24mm; }
    td.text-cell { width: 32.6mm; padding: 3mm 2mm 3mm 1mm; }
    .text-slot { position: relative; width: 32.6mm; height: 24mm; }
    .text-position { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 50%; width: 32.6mm; transform: translateY(-50%); }
    .text-content { width: 32.6mm; max-height: 27.9mm; overflow: hidden; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
    .label-name { font-size: 7.5pt; font-weight: bold; line-height: 1.25; }
    .label-line { font-size: 6.5pt; color: #3f3f46; line-height: 1.3; }
    .label-site { font-size: 6pt; color: #52525b; line-height: 1.3; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  {% for page in labels|batch(24) %}
    <table class="sheet{% if not loop.last %} page-break{% endif %}">
      {% for row in page|batch(3) %}
        <tr>
          {% for label in row %}
            {% if not loop.first %}<td class="gutter"></td>{% endif %}
            <td class="label">
              <table class="label-inner">
                <tr>
                  <td class="qr-cell"><img src="{{ label.qrDataUri }}" alt=""></td>
                  <td class="text-cell">
                    <div class="text-slot"><div class="text-position"><div class="text-content">
                    <div class="label-name">{{ label.type }}{% if label.subType is not empty %} — {{ label.subType }}{% endif %}</div>
                    {% if label.serialNumber is not empty %}
                      <div class="label-line">{{ 'equipmentLabels.serialNumber'|trans({ '%serial%': label.serialNumber }, 'pdf', lang) }}</div>
                    {% endif %}
                    {% if label.facilityName is not empty %}
                      <div class="label-site">{{ label.facilityName }}</div>
                    {% endif %}
                    {% if label.locationLabel is not empty %}
                      <div class="label-site">{{ label.locationLabel }}</div>
                    {% endif %}
                    </div></div></div>
                  </td>
                </tr>
              </table>
            </td>
          {% endfor %}
          {% if row|length < 3 %}
            {% for filler in range(1, 3 - row|length) %}
              <td class="gutter"></td>
              <td class="label"></td>
            {% endfor %}
          {% endif %}
        </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </table>
  {% endfor %}
</body>
</html>
